From c7cc19a982a1383f737e4e04a414ed949e63e63f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:50:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 201/209] refactor(area): Area component attaches the entity's
 native links

The Area component kept its own list of link GUIDs, with a Pick Link Target /
Clear Links tool pair to author it. That reinvented a wheel the engine already
turns: IEntity::GetEntityLinks() / AddEntityLink (IEntity.h:1269-1273,
IEntityLink at :262-268) is the list Sandbox's own Link tool writes, the level
serializes as <EntityLinks>, and CEntityLoadManager::OnBatchCreationCompleted
(EntityLoadManager.cpp:690-711) resolves on load - and every link already
carries BOTH an EntityId and an EntityGUID, which is the whole reason our list
stored GUIDs.

So the component no longer has a list. It has one reflected LinkName (empty
means every link; otherwise only links with that name) and re-syncs the hidden
area proxy's attached list to the entity's links on Initialize, LEVEL_LOADED,
START_GAME, RESET, ENTITY_EVENT_LINK, ENTITY_EVENT_DELINK, LAYER_UNHIDE and
IEntitySystemSink::OnSpawn. A link whose entityId is still 0 - a target in a
layer that was not loaded - is resolved through FindEntityByGuid, the way the
load manager resolves its own queued links, so late layers and late spawns
still link. The host's self-attachment is never touched by the sync.

Two engine details the sync has to respect: DELINK is sent while the link is
still in the list (Entity.cpp:2992, RemoveEntityLink) but after it is unlinked
in RemoveAllEntityLinks (:3021), so the link in nParam[0] is skipped
explicitly; and CEntityObject::UpdateIEntityLinks (EntityObject.cpp:4394)
removes every link and re-adds them on any edit, so the sync arrives in bursts
and must be idempotent - it reconciles rather than appends.

The inspector row is now a read-only count derived from the sync ("2 linked",
"1 linked, 1 not loaded"); links are authored in the entity's own Links
section. Tools/AreaLinkTools.*, Interface/IAreaFunctionComponent.h and the
Area component's editor actions are deleted. The generic
IEditorActionComponent mechanism stays - the shape kinds use it for
"Edit Shape".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
